id: 12
hanzi: 胡说
pinyin: hú shuō
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Verb

meanings_summary:
  en: to talk nonsense; to drivel; to speak rubbish without factual basis
  es: decir tonterías; hablar disparates; hablar sin ton ni son; desvariar

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Verb | Colloquial | to utter statements that are completely untrue, absurd, groundless, or irrational | decir cosas absurdas, falsas, descabelladas o desprovistas de fundamento | 纯属胡说 (sheer nonsense)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 面对毫无事实依据的网络谣言，当事人严正声明这完全是在胡说，并保留法律追责的权利。 | Miànduì háowú shìshí yījù de wǎnglù yáoyán, dāngshìrén yánzhèng shēngmíng zhè wánquán shì zài húshuō, bìng bǎoliú fǎlǜ zhuīzé de quánlì. | Facing internet rumors with zero factual basis, the party solemn declared this was sheer nonsense, reserving the right to seek legal accountability. | Ante los infundados bulos propagados por internet, el afectado declaró con firmeza que se trataba de meras calumnias y se reservó el derecho a emprender acciones legales.
  #2 | 盲人们因各执己见而彼此斥责对方在胡说，这则寓言深刻揭示了主观片面性如何导致无谓的争吵。 | Mángrénmen yīn gèzhíjǐjiàn ér bǐcǐ chìzé duìfāng zài húshuō, zhè zé yùyán shēnkè jiēshì le zhǔguān piànmiànxìng rúhé dǎozhì wúwèi de zhēngchǎo. | Because each clung to their own view, the blind men rebuked each other for talking nonsense, revealing how one-sidedness incites futile discord. | Al aferrarse cada cual a su juicio, los ciegos se reprocharon hablar disparates, mostrando cómo la parcialidad subjetiva desata disputas estériles.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  胡说八道 | talk sheer rubbish; babble drivel
  纯属胡说 | sheer nonsense; total drivel
  简直是胡说 | simply talking utter nonsense
  胡言乱语 | raving nonsense; wild babble
  休得胡说 | stop talking nonsense!
  信口胡说 | blabber wildly without thinking

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  胡说八道 | hú shuō bā dào | talk complete drivel; spout unadulterated nonsense
  信口雌黄 | xìn kǒu cí huáng | make irresponsible remarks; change words arbitrarily
  信口开河 | xìn kǒu kāi hé | talk at random; speak without restraint or facts
  捕风捉影 | bǔ fēng zhuō yǐng | catch at wind and shadows; make groundless accusations

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  胡 | hú | reckless; barbarian; beard; why | imprudente; desordenado; barba | 月 | flesh / moon | 月 (flesh, animal throat dewlap) | 古 (gǔ, ancient / phonetic) | 9 | 左右结构 | Ancient pictogram depicting the hanging dewlap of flesh beneath an ox's chin. Later borrowed phonetically for northern nomads, and figuratively for wild/reckless behavior. | An ancient (古) beast with a loose flap of flesh (月) beneath its neck babbles wildly (胡). | Una criatura con piel colgante (月) y trazas arcaicas (古) que profiere sonidos desordenados (胡). | 35 | JRB | 
  说 | shuō | speak; talk; explain; persuade | hablar; decir; explicar | 讠 | speech / words | 讠 (speech, utterance) | 兑 (duì, exchange / pleasure / mouth) | 9 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: speech radical 讠 combined with joyous mouth 兑, expressing exchanging thoughts through verbal words. | Exchanging words (讠) through a smiling, expressive mouth (兑) conveys human speech (说). | Palabras (讠) que brotan gozosas de una boca abierta (兑) para comunicar el pensamiento hablado (说). | 55 | IVCR | 說

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Speaking (说) in a wild, ungrounded, reckless fashion (胡) amounts to talking pure nonsense (胡说).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Hablar (说) de forma salvaje y sin fundamento (胡) equivale a decir disparates (胡说).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient Han Chinese records, nomadic tribes from northern frontiers were termed 胡 (Hú). Because their languages and customs were unfamiliar to central plains dwellers, words prefixed with 胡 (胡说, 胡思乱想, 胡闹) came to designate speech or actions deemed chaotic, irregular, or absurd.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone followed by high level 1st tone: 'hú shuō' (35-55). Glide up with 'hú', then produce a steady, unvarying high pitch on 'shuō'.

