semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 胡说 is an emphatic colloquial verb expressing that statements are completely fictitious, absurd, or groundless.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 胡说 vs. 瞎说 | xiāshuō | Both mean talking nonsense, but 瞎说 emphasizes speaking without having seen the facts (blind guesswork), while 胡说 emphasizes speaking absurdly, outrageously, or offensively.
    2 | 胡说 vs. 造谣 | zàoyáo | 胡说 can be casual exaggeration or foolish talk, whereas 造谣 is a deliberate, malicious criminal act of manufacturing false rumors to mislead the public.
    3 | 胡说 vs. 撒谎 | sāhuǎng | 胡说 highlights that the words are bizarre, illogical, or unfounded nonsense, whereas 撒谎 specifically means telling a conscious, deliberate lie to deceive.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在人际沟通中，无端的胡说与猜忌最容易摧毁彼此历经岁月建立的深厚信任。遇事多一份理性的求证，少一点轻信与传讹，用真诚的倾听化解误解，人与人之间的交往才能真正回归坦荡与温存。 | Zài rénjì gōutōng zhōng, wúduān de húshuō yǔ cāijì zuì róngyì cuīhuǐ bǐcǐ lìjīng suìyuè jiànlì de shēnhòu xìnrèn. Yùshì duō yí fèn lǐxìng de qiúzhèng, shǎo yìdiǎn qīngxìn yǔ chuán'é, yòng zhēnchéng de qīngtīng huàjiě wùjiě, rén yǔ rén zhījiān de jiāowǎng cáinéng zhēnzhèng huíguī tǎndàng yǔ wēncún. | In interpersonal communication, groundless rubbish and suspicion most easily destroy mutual trust built over years. Seeking rational verification, minimizing credulity, and dissolving misunderstandings through sincere listening allows relationships to remain candid. | En el trato humano, los infundios y sospechas destruyen con facilidad la confianza forjada durante años. Aportar rigor racional, desterrar la ligereza y disolver malentendidos mediante la escucha leal devuelve a la convivencia su noble franqueza.
  #2 | 融媒体时代的网络舆论场极其敏感脆弱，个别自媒体为了追求流量眼球往往信口胡说、扭曲事实真相。建立健全的互联网法治监管机制与事实核查体系，对于净化网络生态空间具有深远意义。 | Róngméitǐ shídài de wǎnglù yúlùnchǎng jíqí mǐngǎn cuìruò, gèbié zìméitǐ wèile zhuīqiú liúliàng yǎnqiú wǎngwǎng xìnkǒu-húshuō, niǔqū shìshí zhēnxiàng. Jiànlì jiànquán de hùliánwǎng fǎzhì jiānguǎn jīzhì yǔ shìshí héchá tǐxì, duìyú jìnghuà wǎnglù shēngtài kōngjiān jùyǒu shēnyuǎn yìyì. | In the convergence media era, online public opinion is fragile; certain creators spout drivel and distort truth merely to chase clicks. Establishing robust legal oversight and fact-checking systems carries profound significance for purifying cyberspace. | En la era digital, la opinión pública en redes es vulnerable; creadores irresponsables vierten falsedades distorsionando la realidad por ganar clics. Erigir un marco regulatorio eficaz y mecanismos de verificación es crucial para sanear el ecosistema informativo en línea.
